@* Batch UX-1 (CAT-SCRIPT-1, mid-batch owner addendum, verbatim: "When we go
   to catechism frontiers, and we have THE SCRIPTURES ... i want the
   structure to be <TITLE> <Passage ref> and then verses below. so on the
   first commandment, i would want to see God Alone as Judge on the left,
   in bigger, more readable letters than it is in its current state, and
   LUK.12.13-14 on the right and keep the font."): the reusable title+ref
   HEADER ROW for a passage-list entry that carries a caption/title --
   PassageList.razor's own CatechismScripturesSection consumer is the
   first user (the First Commandment's "God Alone as Judge" / LUK.12.13-14
   pairing is the named, screenshot-judged fixture), but this is a
   standalone component precisely so any OTHER section pairing a title
   with a passage ref can compose it without a parallel implementation --
   THE COMPOSABILITY BAR, extended by controller ruling to this header's
   own type scale (ONE token, --passage-title-size, app.css, below --
   "changing the clamp should be literally one line of code," the owner's
   own words, applied here to "changing the title's size").

   TITLE left (bigger/more readable than the old plain-italic caption --
   see .popover-passage-title's own app.css comment), REF right (KEEPS its
   existing font/class -- .popover-passage-ref-label, UNCHANGED, "keep the
   font" per the owner's own words verbatim) -- a plain flex row,
   space-between, so DOM order (title first, ref second) alone produces
   the left/right layout with no positioning trick either side needs to
   know about. *@
<div class="popover-passage-header">
    <span class="popover-passage-title" data-testid="@TitleTestId">@Title</span>
    <span class="popover-passage-ref-label" data-testid="@RefTestId">@Ref</span>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Ref { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string TitleTestId { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string RefTestId { get; set; } = default!;
}
